{
  "bridge_text": "With the queen's light flickering like a dying ember, the weight of Mosk's old regret hung heavy in the air. Lina moved closer to see if their presence could finally bring a change.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "The firefly's light pulsed weakly, a dim rhythm against the dark bark of the hollow. Mosk stood frozen, his paws trembling, remembering the winter he failed her. He had guarded this tree in silence, hoping for a chance to make amends, but fear had kept him from stepping into the light."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied. The humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before — and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
